About_Management_ISU:'Management of INTEGRATED SET-UP (ISU)',
Body1_Management_ISU:'1. Directorate of Land Records and Surveys , West Bengal implements the Integrated Setup of Land Reforms Administration at different administrative levels in each district and looks after the works relating to the ISU. it functions under the overall control, supervision and guidance of Department in general and Land Reforms Commissioner in particular.<br/><br/>2. The Directorate issues technical instructions, subject to guidelines, if any, that may be issued by the Department from time to time, to be followed in technical matters including preparation on revision of maps, land-survey etc.<br/><br/> 3. Director of Land Records &amp; Survey (DLR&amp;S) West Bengal has the responsibility of drawing up the work programme for the districts and supervise, control and monitor the performance with the overall objective of obtaining the optimum output from the workforce. He is also responsible for implementation of land reforms measures in the state. He plans, organize and carry out the preparation or revision of record-of- rights, subject to instruction, that may be issued by the Land and Land Reforms Department from time to time, within such time-limit as may be prescribed by the Department.<br/><br/> ',
Body2_Management_ISU:'4. <b><ins>Maintenance of Gradation List</ins></b> <br/> DLRS,WB maintains gradation lists of the following cadres. Provisional /Draft Gradation Lists are published annually on the basis of which promotions are offered.',
Body3_Management_ISU:'5. The Department maintains the Gradation Lists of Revenue Officers , Special Revenue Officer, Grade II and Special Revenue Officer, Grade II',


