	indobangladesh:'indobangladesh.png',
	Land_Acquisition_Head:'Various types of Work done in LAND ACQUISITION BRANCH',
	Land_Acquisition_Body:'The duties of LA Branch is related to Land Acquisition Work under LA Act of 1894(Act-1), WB (Acquisition & Requisition) Act 1948(Act-II). the NHAI Act, 1956, Railways Act, <br>P & MP Act, 1962(for GA1L Projects), etc.<br><br>As Act I is not in force and Act II has already been repealed, acquisition is made through Direct Purchase Policy issued vide this Department No. 756-LP/I A-03/14(Pt-II) dated 25.02.2016. A committee has been formed at the district level for this purpose.<br><br>LA Branch has to monitor a huge number of LA related Court Cases in different District Courts as well as High Court at Calcutta and Apex Court. LA Branch has to examine the decreetal estimates following the judgment passed by Hon&apos;ble Courts and decide either to approve it or appeal against the judgment.<br><br>In addition to above the following matters are dealt with in this Branch.<br><br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;1.	Land Development Scheme (Baishnabghata, Sodepur, Purba Putiary).<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;2.	Deed of Transfer and arbitration.<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;3.	Temporary Acquisition in favour of IOCL.<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;4.	RTI related to LA matter.<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;5.	Relinquishment of acquired land.<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;6.	Payment of LA compensation through LOK-Adalat<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;7.	Petition regarding non receipt of LA Compensation.<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;8.	8. Land Acquisition for BSF.<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;9.	GIS mapping of land.',
	Land_Collector_Head:'Functions and Mandate of the office of the First Land Acquisition Collector, Kolkata',
	Land_Collector_Body:'The First Land Acquisition Collector, Kolkata has been operating office from 5, Bankshall Street, Kolkata, since pre independence.<br><br>The functions and mandates of this office are as follows:<br>&bull;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;	 Requisition and Acquisition of premises and land for Central and State Govt. Offices and other public purposes. The mandate of exercising its  jurisdiction in relation to acquisition of land has been re defined in 1995 and presently the office of the First Land Acquisition Collector is  operating within the jurisdiction of following 28 Police Stations ( as in 1995) in Kolkata:Shyampukur, Jorabagan, Burtola, Burrabazar, Jorasnako, Amherst Street, Hare Street, Bowbazar, Muchipara,Taltala, Park Street, Hastings, Cossipore, Chitpur, Bullygunj, Gariahat, Alipore, Bhowanipore, Karaya, Manicktala, Ultandanga, Beliaghata, Phulbagan, Narkeldanga, Beniapukur, Tangra, Entally, North Port.<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&bull;&nbsp;	To support the rail and road transportation system of the governments by way of acquisition of land on behalf of Kolkata Metro, East West Metro, Public Works  Department, KMDA, Transport Department etc.<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&bull;&nbsp;	To determine Reasonable Rent for Government Offices on private premises occupied by the Central and State Government and vice-versa as per existing G.O. of L. &L.R. Deptt.<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&bull;&nbsp;	This office is also engaged in establishment of hundreds of Educational Institutions, Medical Centres and other government institutions by way of requisition and acquisition of land on their (Requiring Body) behalf.<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&bull;&nbsp;	This office also provides premises and land by acquisition and requisition to Kolkata Municipal Corporation, KMDA, Kolkata Police, to facilitate the better public service in the State Capital.<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&bull;&nbsp;	Furthermore, this office has also been performing very vital role in implementing the Land Development and Planning and other Acts for Rehabilitation of Refugees in and around Kolkata.<br><br>This office deals with the following Acts:<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;1)&nbsp;	Land Acquisition Act, 1894,<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;2)&nbsp;	Defence of India Act 1939,<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;3)&nbsp;	W.B. Premises Requisition (Temporary Provisions) Act, 1947,<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;4)&nbsp;	Continuance of Power Act, 1948,<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;5)&nbsp;	W.B. Land Development & Planning Act, 1948,<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;6)&nbsp;	W.B. Land (Requisition & Acquisition) Act, 1948,<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;7)&nbsp;	Requisition and Acquisition of Immovable Property Act, 1952,<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;8)&nbsp;	Public Premises (Eviction of Unauthorized Occupants) Act, 1962/1971,<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;9)&nbsp;	New L.A. Act, 2013, <br><br>One of the major activities of the office in the recent times has been to monitor the various court cases arising out of acquisition and requisition of premises and land under the above acts.  Minor activities include:<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;1.&nbsp;	e-governance, by computerizing/scanning the existing files <br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;2.&nbsp;	 Other  day to day office activities ',
	
