	lbl_SOP_for_industrial_Mutation:'SoP for disposal of Mutation',
	lbl_SOP_for_industrial_Conversion:'SoP for disposal of Conversion',
	lbl_SOP_for_industrial_conv_para:'1.	The petitioner will submit conversion application annexing all required documents as mentioned in the Department circular no: 324-LP/1A-12/13 dated 5th Feb, 2015.<br><br>2.	At the time of submission, all the documents will properly be checked and if any defect is/are found, then that will be informed to the concerned petitioners.<br>&nbsp;  	The petitioner will submit the documents within three (03) days.<br><br>3.	If the petition is found in order then that will be sent for field enquiry and enquiring officer should inform the date to the petitioner.<br><br>4.	After physical verification, the Collector under 4C of the WBLR Act will take a hearing and dispose of the case on merit.<br><br>5.	As directed in the circular, the entire process must be completed by 30 days from the date of receipt of the petition.<br><br>6.	Documents required for filing Conversion petition are mentioned in Department Circular no. 324-LP/1A-12/13 dated 5th Feb, 2015<br><br>',
	lbl_SOP_for_industrial_mute_para:'1.	Automated mutation system has been started. After completion of registration in the Registration Office, deed will be electronically transmitted to the BL&LRO Office.<br>&nbsp; There is no need to file separate mutation petition.<br><br>2.	Cases where, vendor is the recorded owner of the land, no hearing or enquiry will be conducted. Name of the vendee/vendees will automatically be mutated in the RoRs.<br>&nbsp;  The vendee will get an intimation through his registered mobile no.<br><br>3.	For other types of cases, usual reference be made to the ULC/LA and if no reply is received within 14 days, then it will be presumed that there is no objection in granting the mutation.<br><br>4.	In no circumstance, the disposal of mutation should not exceed 60 days.<br><br>',
